    {
      "id": "ISA.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the year that king Uzziah died I saw also the LORD sitting upon a throne, high and elevated, and his train filled the temple.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Above it stood seraphim: each one had six wings; with two he covered his face, and with two he covered his feet, and with two he flew.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And one cried to another, and said, Holy, holy, holy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD of hosts: the whole earth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " full of his glory.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the posts of the door moved at the voice of him that cried, and the house was filled with smoke.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said I, Woe ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " me! for I am undone; because I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a man of unclean lips, and I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips: for my eyes have seen the King, the LORD of hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then one of the seraphim flew to me, having a live coal in his hand, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he had taken with the tongs from off the altar:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he laid ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon my mouth, and said, Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thy iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also I heard the voice of the LORD, saying, Whom shall I send, and who will go for us? Then said I, Here ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I; send me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Go, and tell this people, Hear ye indeed, but understand not; and see ye indeed, but perceive not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make the heart of this people fat, and make their ears heavy, and shut their eyes; lest they see with their eyes, and hear with their ears, and understand with their heart, and convert, and be healed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said I, Lord, how long? And he answered, Until the cities shall be wasted without inhabitant, and the houses without man, and the land be utterly desolate;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
